Add a Negotiate proxy-auth patch to the rsu feed's azure-c-shared-utility package.

The Azure SDK's curl-based HTTP adapter only sets CURLOPT_PROXYUSERPWD, which
limits proxy authentication to Basic. Add a second patch (002-...) that also
sets CURLOPT_PROXYAUTH to CURLAUTH_NEGOTIATE | CURLAUTH_BASIC so libcurl can
satisfy proxies that require Kerberos/SPNEGO (with Basic kept as a fallback).

This is the DPS / HTTPS code path. The MQTT-over-WSS path lives in
http_proxy_io.c and needs a separate, larger patch.

Refreshed for c-utility at LTS_03_2025 (SHA 772a4f8b): the line offset moved
(was ~843, now ~820) and the authLen computation now uses safe_add_size_t.
Context updated accordingly; the inserted block is unchanged.

diff --git a/libs/azure-c-shared-utility/patches/002-enable-negotiate-proxy-auth.patch b/libs/azure-c-shared-utility/patches/002-enable-negotiate-proxy-auth.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libs/azure-c-shared-utility/patches/002-enable-negotiate-proxy-auth.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+--- a/adapters/httpapi_curl.c
++++ b/adapters/httpapi_curl.c
+@@ -817,6 +817,12 @@
+                 }
+                 else
+                 {
++                    /* Negotiate (Kerberos/SPNEGO) proxy auth, falling back to Basic.
++                     * Curl picks whichever scheme the proxy advertises in 407 responses.
++                     * Ignore CURLE_NOT_BUILT_IN: if curl lacks GSSAPI, Basic still works. */
++                    (void)curl_easy_setopt(httpHandleData->curl, CURLOPT_PROXYAUTH,
++                                           CURLAUTH_NEGOTIATE | CURLAUTH_BASIC);
++
+                     if (proxy_data->username != NULL && proxy_data->password != NULL)
+                     {
+                         size_t authLen = safe_add_size_t(strlen(proxy_data->username), strlen(proxy_data->password));
